   "updated_at": "2026-06-23T09:11:39Z",
   "body": "Thanks for the report. #4890 changed this to align Base UI\u2019s computed validity with native constraint validation: disabled controls are excluded from validation/submission and a disabled `<input>` matches neither `:valid` nor `:invalid`.\n\nThe `invalid` prop is a separate case, though. It\u2019s an app-controlled signal rather than browser constraint validation, so disabling the field likely should not hide that explicit invalid state. I think we should keep computed validity suppressed while disabled, but still emit `data-invalid` for an explicitly invalid disabled field.\n\nIs there a concrete use case for surfacing invalid state on a disabled field? Since browsers don\u2019t expose this through `:invalid`, it\u2019d help to know how you\u2019re relying on it, for example disabling a form during submit while a value is still flagged.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "pin": null,
